<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Altava</h1><p class="st-meta">578 CE – 708 CE (approx.) · capital Altava</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Christian Berber kingdom of western Algeria whose king Kusaila killed the Arab conqueror Uqba ibn Nafi.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garmul">Garmul</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-moors-and-romans">Kingdom of the Moors and Romans</a> in 578, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> rulers continued to hold the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altava">Altava</a> and the plains of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. By the 7th century the dominant group was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awraba">Awraba</a>, a Berber confederation whose leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a> (Kasila) was Christian.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Almost nothing is known of the kingdom between 578 and the 680s. Arab writers say <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a> was captured by the commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-al-muhajir-dinar">Abu al-Muhajir</a>, converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and accompanied the Arab army, but was humiliated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi">Uqba ibn Nafi</a>. In 682 or 683 he ambushed and killed Uqba at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vescera">Tahuda</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biskra">Biskra</a>, then took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> for several years.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a> was killed around 688 to 690 in battle against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zuhayr-ibn-qays">Zuhayr ibn Qays</a>, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> subdued the region by 708. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awraba">Awraba</a> converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> and later welcomed Idris I at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volubilis">Volubilis</a>, helping found the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-altava.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Altava" width="320" height="238"><figcaption>Image: Naslechat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romano-Berber_Kingdoms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>578 CE – 708 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Altava</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kusaila</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/morocco">Morocco</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Kusaila, Awraba kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=643&amp;focus=kingdom-of-altava" aria-label="Kingdom of Altava on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4654 915 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Altava lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4974 1171L4974 1171M4974 1171L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4974 1171h0M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4974 1171h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4974 1171h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Altava. <a href="/atlas?year=643&amp;focus=kingdom-of-altava">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
